    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: User clarified that clearance constraints must always be enforced (even in Emergency) and admin credential update must be forced at Emergency exit, so the model must be adjusted to enforce these requirements and remove Emergency-mode exceptions for these constraints.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Counterexamples\n- Instances: Meaningful\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===\nStatus: FALSE\nReasoning: Assertion failures remain and the model's Emergency-mode logic does not yet fully enforce the clarified requirements; further targeted fixes are required.\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n1. Clearance Constraint in Emergency:\n   - Remove or revise any model logic (assertions, facts, guards) that allow processor clearance requirements to be relaxed in Emergency mode.\n   - Ensure the clearance requirement applies identically in both Normal and Emergency modes.\n   - Example: In all assertions and facts involving processor clearance, eliminate any special cases for Emergency mode.\n   - Code:\n     ```alloy\n     all s: State, r: Request | \n         s.reqStatus[r] = Processed and some s.reqProcessor[r] =>\n             let proc = s.reqProcessor[r], rc = requestClassification[r] |\n                 leqClearance[rc, proc.clearance]\n     ```\n2. Admin Credential Update Timing:\n   - Modify the transition logic such that all administrators’ credentials are automatically updated exactly once upon transition from Emergency to Normal mode.\n   - Prevent admin credential updates at any other point or multiple times per Emergency period.\n   - Code:\n     ```alloy\n     all s, s2: State |\n         s.mode = Emergency and s2.mode = Normal and Next[s, s2] =>\n             all a: Administrator | s2.adminCredUpdated[a] = True\n     all s, s2: State, a: Administrator |\n         not (s.mode = Emergency and s2.mode = Normal and Next[s, s2]) =>\n             s2.adminCredUpdated[a] = s.adminCredUpdated[a]\n     ```\n3. Emergency FIFO Bypass:\n   - Ensure Emergency-mode FIFO bypass logic does not override or weaken the clearance constraint.\n   - Emergency mode may bypass request order, but all other constraints (including clearance) must remain enforced.\n   - Update relevant facts or scenario predicates to reflect this.\n4. Mutex and Other Emergency-mode Exceptions:\n   - Confirm that only mutex constraints are relaxed in Emergency; do not relax clearance or admin update constraints.\n   - Audit all Emergency-mode exception logic and guard only those aspects explicitly permitted.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\n- Assumption: \"Request processor clearance constraint is enforced in all modes.\"\n  - Category: confirm\n  - Rationale: User explicitly confirmed; encode as an invariant across all modes.\n- Assumption: \"Administrators must immediately update credentials after Emergency exit.\"\n  - Category: confirm\n  - Rationale: User confirmed update is to be forced automatically at Emergency exit.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\nNone - requirements are clear\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nQ1: confirmed - User clarified that processor clearance is always enforced, even in Emergency.\nQ2: confirmed - User clarified that admin credential update must be forced at Emergency exit.\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Remove Emergency-mode clearance exceptions and enforce clearance constraint in all modes.\n- Update admin credential update logic to force update automatically at Emergency exit only.\n- Audit Emergency-mode exception logic to ensure only mutex is relaxed; all other constraints remain enforced.\n\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): \n- Ensure Emergency FIFO bypass cannot violate the clearance constraint.\n- Verify that no other Emergency-mode exceptions are unintentionally allowed.\n\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): \n- After corrections, add negative and edge-case checks to confirm model adequacy and prevent future regressions.\n```",
