    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: User clarified stricter requirements for emergency processing and role management, necessitating refinement of model constraints and immediate repair of identified logic.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Unsatisfiable\n- Combined Model: Unsatisfiable\n- Assertions: Counterexamples\n- Instances: N/A\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===\nStatus: FALSE\nReasoning: Hard metrics do not pass; user has clarified stricter requirements and requested additional constraints and scenario coverage.\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n1. Emergency Processing Logic:\n   - Update the EmergencyProcessingPriority fact to require that during Emergency mode, all high-classification requests are processed simultaneously before any medium requests, and all medium requests are then processed simultaneously before any low requests. No request of a lower classification may be processed until all higher classifications are completed.\n     - Example fix:\n       ```alloy\n       fact EmergencyProcessingPriority {\n         all s, s2: State |\n           (s.mode = Emergency and s.next = s2) =>\n             (\n               // Only high requests may transition from Pending to Processed until all high are done\n               (some r: Request | r.class = High and s.reqStatus[r] = Pending) =>\n                 all r: Request |\n                   (s.reqStatus[r] = Pending and s2.reqStatus[r] = Processed) => r.class = High\n               // Only medium requests may transition after all high are processed\n               else (some r: Request | r.class = Med and s.reqStatus[r] = Pending) =>\n                 all r: Request |\n                   (s.reqStatus[r] = Pending and s2.reqStatus[r] = Processed) => r.class = Med\n               // Only low requests after high and medium are done\n               else\n                 all r: Request |\n                   (s.reqStatus[r] = Pending and s2.reqStatus[r] = Processed) => r.class = Low\n             )\n       }\n       ```\n     - Adjust the scenario predicates/tests so they validate this behavior step-wise.\n\n2. Role Assignment Persistence:\n   - Ensure that all assigned roles to users remain active and consistent throughout all time steps. No automatic role removal or deactivation is permitted.\n     - Review facts/predicates for unintended role changes across states.\n     - Example:\n       ```alloy\n       fact RolePersistence {\n         all s, s2: State, u: User, r: Role |\n           (s.next = s2) => (r in s.userRoles[u] iff r in s2.userRoles[u])\n       }\n       ```\n\n3. Delegation and Approval Constraints:\n   - Add facts to enforce:\n     - A user cannot delegate a role to himself.\n       ```alloy\n       fact NoSelfDelegation {\n         all s: State, u: User, r: Role |\n           (u -> r) not in s.delegations[u]\n       }\n       ```\n     - A user cannot approve his own requests.\n       ```alloy\n       fact NoSelfApproval {\n         all s: State, r: Request |\n           s.requestor[r] != s.processor[r]\n       }\n       ```\n     - There must be a record of the request processor for each processed request to enable verification.\n       ```alloy\n       fact ProcessorRecord {\n         all s: State, r: Request |\n           s.reqStatus[r] = Processed => some s.processor[r]\n       }\n       ```\n\n4. Mutex Constraints:\n   - Review all facts enforcing role mutex; ensure mutex is only enforced in Normal mode and not during Emergency.\n   - Update assertion/assertMutexAllowedDuringEmergency and test witnesses accordingly.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\n- Assumption: Emergency mode allows concurrent processing of all requests of a given classification only (not mixed-class or partial).\n  - Category: confirm\n  - Rationale: Directly stated in user clarification; should be enforced strictly in model.\n\n- Assumption: All assigned roles must persist and remain active at all times.\n  - Category: confirm\n  - Rationale: Explicit user requirement; model must guarantee role persistence.\n\n- Assumption: No self-delegation or self-approval permitted.\n  - Category: confirm\n  - Rationale: User explicitly states these are forbidden; must be added as facts.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Clarify (in formal requirements/specification) that:\n  1. In Emergency mode, all requests of a given classification (High, then Med, then Low) must be processed together before any lower classification is handled.\n  2. Role assignments are persistent and always active.\n  3. Self-delegation and self-approval are prohibited.\n  4. A processor record is required for each processed request.\n- Update documentation and requirements to explicitly reflect these points.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Update EmergencyProcessingPriority logic for strict class-based batch processing during Emergency mode.\n- Enforce persistent role assignments across all time steps.\n- Add facts prohibiting self-delegation and self-approval; require processor records.\n- Review and scope mutex enforcement for Emergency mode.\n\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): \n- Update and rerun all relevant scenarios and assertions to cover new/clarified requirements.\n- Confirm that all new constraints are correctly captured and that no regressions are introduced.\n\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): \n- Add negative/vacuity/edge-case checks after all hard metrics and clarified requirements pass.\n```",
